# Async Patterns and Promise Handling Rules

## Async/Await Usage

- Prefer async/await over promises
- Use async/await for sequential operations
- Use Promise.all for parallel operations
- Handle async errors properly
- Use proper async function signatures

## Promise Patterns

- Avoid Promise chains when async/await is clearer
- Use Promise.all for concurrent operations
- Use Promise.race for timeout patterns
- Handle promise rejections properly
- Avoid creating unnecessary promises

## VSCode API Async Patterns

- Use await for VSCode API calls
- Handle editor operations asynchronously
- Use proper async patterns for file operations
- Handle workspace operations asynchronously
- Use async patterns for user interactions

## Error Handling in Async Code

- Use try-catch only when necessary for async operations
- Handle async errors at appropriate levels
- Provide user feedback for async failures
- Use proper error propagation
- Handle timeout scenarios

## Performance Considerations

- Use Promise.all for independent operations
- Avoid blocking async operations
- Use proper cancellation patterns
- Handle memory leaks in async code
- Use debouncing for user input

## Common Patterns

- Use async functions for command handlers
- Handle editor operations asynchronously
- Use proper async patterns for file I/O
- Handle user interactions asynchronously
- Use async patterns for API calls

